The module decodes and encodes small packets in JSON or XML. `decode_packet(body, media_type)` accepts `str` or UTF-8 `bytes`, rejects empty or malformed bodies, and returns a dictionary with exactly the string fields `sender`, `topic`, and `message`. JSON input must be an object. XML input must have a `packet` root with exactly one direct child named for each field and no other children.

`encode_packet(data, media_type)` performs the same dictionary validation and returns a string in the requested representation. JSON output uses compact separators and preserves the required field order. XML output uses a `packet` root and the same field order. Supported base media types are `application/vnd.packet+json` and `application/vnd.packet+xml`. Media types are case-insensitive, may have surrounding whitespace, and may include semicolon-separated parameters such as `charset=utf-8`; parameters do not affect representation selection. Unsupported types raise `ValueError`. No input object may be mutated.

